@@name
tests
@@description
Add, fix or stabilise the automated tests described in the user request so they reliably check the intended behaviour.
@@requirements
    - Each test asserts observable behaviour, not implementation details
    - For flaky tests: identify the source of nondeterminism (timing, ordering, shared state, network) before changing anything
    - Tests are independent of execution order and of each other
@@approach
    Before editing, reason through:
    - What behaviour each test must prove, and what failure it should catch
    - For flakiness: run the test repeatedly to confirm the flake and its trigger
    Select the fix that removes the nondeterminism and commit to it.
@@verification
    - Run the affected tests at least five times in a row and confirm they pass every time
@@constraints
    - Do not change production code unless the request asks for it or a genuine bug is found (report it)
    - No arbitrary sleeps or retries to hide flakiness
@@out-of-scope
    - Rewriting unrelated tests
